			"date": "2024-02-20T11:46:27.000Z",
			"content": "<h3><a></a>Top Links</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"http://feed.azuredevops.show/kent-beck-tidy-first-episode-285\">Kent Beck: Tidy First – Azure DevOps Podcast Episode 285</a> (Jeffrey Palermo)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.telerik.com/blogs/exploring-4-behaviors-net-maui-community-toolkit\">Beyond the Basics: Exploring 4 Behaviors from the .NET MAUI Community Toolkit</a> (Leomaris Reyes)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://blog.jetbrains.com/dotnet/2024/02/19/jetbrains-rider-and-the-net-aspire-plugin/\">JetBrains Rider and the .NET Aspire Plugin</a> (Khalid Abuhakmeh)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/dotnet/wpf/blob/main/roadmap.md\">WPF Roadmap Updated</a> (Pankaj Chaurasia)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/dotnet/developing-optimized-github-actions-with-net-and-native-aot/\">Developing Optimized GitHub Actions with .NET and Native AOT</a> (David Pine)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3><a></a>Web &amp; Cloud Development</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://techwatching.dev/posts/azure-sdk-di\">Using dependency injection with Azure .NET SDK</a> (Alexandre Nedelec)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://andrewlock.net/using-named-pipes-with-aspnetcore-and-httpclient/\">Using named pipes with ASP.NET Core and HttpClient</a> (Andrew Lock)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://geoffgraham.me/css-meditation-4-select-style-adjust-select-style-adjust-select-sty/\">CSS Meditation #4: Select, style, adjust. Select, style, adjust. Select, sty…</a> (Geoff Graham)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://dotneteers.net/scaling-applications-in-azure-basic-strategies/\">Scaling Applications in Azure: Basic Strategies</a> (Peter Smulovics)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/web/throbber/\">throbber Web Component</a> (Zach Leatherman)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://auth0.com/blog/get-started-with-auth0-terraform-provider/\">Get Started with the Auth0 Terraform Provider</a> (Deepu K. Sasidharan)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3><a></a>WinUI, .NET MAUI &amp; XAML</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://egvijayanand.in/2024/02/19/dotnet-maui-nightly-builds/\">.NET MAUI – Nightly Builds</a> (Vijay Anand E G)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3><a></a>Visual Studio &amp; .NET</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://code-maze.com/csharp-parallel-foreachasync-and-task-run-with-when-all/\">Parallel.ForEachAsync() and Task.Run() With When.All in C#</a> (Aneta Muslic)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://hackernoon.com/avoiding-memory-leaks-with-weak-events-in-c?source=rss\">Avoiding Memory Leaks with Weak Events in C#</a> <em>and</em> <a href=\"https://hackernoon.com/how-to-use-google-sheets-in-c?source=rss\">How To Use Google Sheets in C#</a> (Nick Cosentino)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://steven-giesel.com/blogPost/9994b00c-8bc2-4794-ae74-80e6ee4cd5e5\">Avoid multiple boolean parameters</a> (Steven Giesel)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/oldnewthing/20240219-00/?p=109424\">Why can’t I trigger a manual blue screen crash by injecting the magic key sequence?</a> (Raymond Chen)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3><a></a>Design, Methodology, AI &amp; Testing</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://aistorybuilders.com/ViewBlogPost/3002\">Upgrading AIStoryBuilders</a> (Michael Washington)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3><a></a>Mobile, IoT &amp; Game Development</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://medium.com/flutter/how-flutter-facilitates-collaboration-between-designers-and-developers-at-l-r-05ec82c9f45e?source=rss----4da7dfd21a33---4\">How Flutter facilitates collaboration between designers and developers at L+R</a> (Ivan Leider)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3><a></a>Screencasts &amp; Videos</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3NFBD3DRbuQ\">Talks Tech #57 – Maureen Josephine – Flutter, Mobile, and Job Relocation From Kenya to Germany</a> (Women Who Code)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3><a></a>Podcasts</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://revisionpath.com/katrina-lenzly\">Revision Path – Katrina Lenzly</a> (Maurice Cherry)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://scrummastertoolbox.libsyn.com/collaboration-over-isolated-performance-lessons-learned-as-a-scrum-product-owner-johannes-andersen\">Scrum Master Toolbox Podcast – Collaboration Over Isolated Performance, Lessons Learned as a Scrum Product Owner | Johannes Andersen</a> (Vasco Duarte)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://powershell.org/2024/02/the-powershell-podcast-reaching-the-summit-grahams-onramp-journey/\">The PowerShell Podcast – Reaching the Summit: Graham’s OnRamp Journey</a> (James Petty)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://syntax.fm/732\">Syntax Podcast Episode 732: Stop going to Spam: DMARC, SPF and DKIM Explained</a> (Wes Bos &amp; Scott Tolinski)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://cloudsecuritypodcast.libsyn.com/ep160-dont-cloud-your-judgement-security-and-cloud-migration-again\">Google Cloud Security Podcast Episode 160 – Don’t Cloud Your Judgement: Security and Cloud Migration, Again!</a> (Anton A. Chuvakin)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://changelog.com/news/82\">The Changelog News Podcast – Quantum computing gets a reality check</a> (Jerod Santo)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://blog.scottlogic.com/2024/02/19/beyond-the-hype-can-technology-sustainability-really-make-a-difference.html\">Beyond the Hype: Can technology sustainability really make a difference?</a> (Colin Eberhardt)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://oasisofcourage.com/156-why-some-engineers-should-definitely-start-a-consulting-business-with-jay-aigner/\">The Happy Engineer Podcast #156: Why Some Engineers Should Definitely Start a Consulting Business with Jay Aigner</a> (Max Ahumada)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3><a></a>Community &amp; Events</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://www.visitphilly.com/features/liberty-bell-awards/\">The Inaugural Visit Philadelphia Liberty Bell Awards</a> (Visit Philly)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3><a></a>PowerShell</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://www.itprotoday.com/powershell/powershell-parameter-validation-ensuring-valid-input-functions\">PowerShell Parameter Validation: Ensuring Valid Input for Functions</a> (Brien Posey)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3><a></a>Miscellaneous</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://blog.ploeh.dk/2024/02/19/extracting-data-from-a-small-csv-file-with-haskell/\">Extracting data from a small CSV file with Haskell</a> (Mark Seemann)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3><a></a>More Link Collections</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://blog.cwa.me.uk/2024/02/20/the-morning-brew-3885/\">The Morning Brew #3885</a> (Chris Alcock)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://samestuffdifferentday.net/2024/02/19/Interesting-links-of-the-week-2024-8/\">Interesting links of the week 2024-8</a> (Michael Eaton)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3><a></a>The Geek Shelf</h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/1835089984/?tag=amavin-20\"><img align=\"left\" style=\"margin:0px 4px 0px 0px;border:0px;float:left;background-image:none;\" src=\"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51WbrSz58FL._SS135_.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"51WbrSz58FL._SS135_.jpg\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/1835089984/?tag=amavin-20\">Refactoring with C#: Safely improve .NET applications and pay down technical debt with Visual Studio, .NET 8, and C# 12</a> (Matt Eland)<em> – Referral Link</em></p>",
